 "captions": {
  "transcript": "audio/transcript.txt",
  "words": "audio/words_aligned.json",
  "groups": [
   "He rose from an artillery officer",
   "to become the most feared / ruler in Europe.",
   "Napoleon Bonaparte crowned himself",
   "Emperor of the French / in 1804.",
   "His armies won / extraordinary victories,",
   "and his empire / reshaped the continent.",
   "But Napoleon wanted more.",
   "In 1812, he invaded Russia",
   "with a vast / multinational army.",
   "He reached Moscow,",
   "only to find much of the city / burning.",
   "Then came the retreat.",
   "Hunger, disease, exhaustion,",
   "and bitter cold / devastated his forces.",
   "His enemies united.",
   "In 1814, Napoleon abdicated",
   "and was exiled to Elba.",
   "He returned the following year",
   "for one final gamble.",
   "At Waterloo, / his army was defeated.",
   "This time, exile meant / a remote island in the Atlantic:",
   "Saint Helena.",
   "Napoleon died there / in 1821.",
   "He conquered kingdoms, / changed Europe,",
   "and became a legend.",
   "But he could not conquer",
   "the consequences / of his own ambition."
  ],
  "style": "outline",
  "size": 60
